# {{.GameName}}

A standalone single-player game built on the Ironwail-Go engine
(github.com/darkliquid/ironwail-go/sdk).

## Layout

- `gameconfig.go` — the game's identity (`sdk.Config`): name, base data
  directory, registration gate. Edit it first.
- `progs/` — QuakeGo gameplay sources (compiled to `progs.dat` by
  `cmd/qgo`; also build as plain Go for sim tests).
- `game_test.go` — simulation tests run by `qcmod test` / `go test` using
  the `quake/sim` headless world (no engine boot needed).

## Commands

```sh
go mod tidy        # resolve quake + engine module replaces
go test ./...      # run the sim tests
make build         # build the game binary
make run           # build + run (from the parent dir, where ./<modname> is
                   # found; game data is loaded from ./<modname>)
```

## Adding game data

Drop the game's `progs.dat`, `maps/`, `gfx/`, and other Quake data into a
`<modname>/` directory next to this one (or inside it as `./<modname>` from
the parent). The engine mounts `<modname>` as its base game directory.